Feature: 4h MACD Momentum
  Primary timeframe: 4h
  Parameter vol_period default 20
  Parameter atr_period default 100
  Parameter atr_mult default 2.5

  # 4h bars (smoother than 1h, denser than daily). All four MACD primitives
  # drive entries/exits, confirmed by above-average volume, protected by a
  # volatility stop frozen at the fill (INC2 atr_value). Pyramiding is enabled
  # in the config, so a repeat signal while in a position adds to it. Because
  # atr_value(atr_period) only warms after 100 bars, the earliest qualifying signals are
  # suppressed and listed in the report's "Suppressed entries" diagnostics.

  Background:
    Given a series avg_vol defined as avg_volume(vol_period)

  Scenario: Enter long on a MACD bullish cross with strong volume
    Given no open position
    When macd_bullish_cross()
    And volume is above avg_vol
    Then long_entry
    And with stop_loss at entry_price - atr_mult * atr_value(atr_period)

  Scenario: Exit long when MACD crosses below zero
    Given a long position is open
    When macd_zero_cross_down()
    Then long_exit

  Scenario: Enter short on a MACD bearish cross with strong volume
    Given no open position
    When macd_bearish_cross()
    And volume is above avg_vol
    Then short_entry
    And with stop_loss at entry_price + atr_mult * atr_value(atr_period)

  Scenario: Exit short when MACD crosses above zero
    Given a short position is open
    When macd_zero_cross_up()
    Then short_exit
